{"id": "EUVD-2026-107538", "enisaUuid": "92daee95-6430-391a-8763-335dbb0aacf5", "description": "Apache Traffic Server can crash with a null pointer dereference when a client POST request is torn down via half-close while a chunked origin response is being reparsed from a reentrant write-ready callback, a timing-dependent race introduced by the CVE-2021-32564 flow-control backports.\n\n\n\nThis issue affects Apache Traffic Server: 9.2.15, 10.1.4, 10.2.0.\n\n\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 9.2.16, 10.1.5, or 10.2.1, which fix the issue.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T19:20:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T19:20:38", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://lists.apache.org/thread/r95dq29ywcd1f4x30snxlqmb12z4s4kc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112381", "GHSA-vv7x-cx95-rcmh"], "assigner": "apache", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "16762b02-2cf7-379d-9bf9-e59b41b37774", "product": {"name": "Apache Traffic Server", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "10.1.4"}, {"id": "b867ea31-37e7-358b-a6a6-5ff2df81e782", "product": {"name": "Apache Traffic Server", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "10.2.0"}, {"id": "e665ad1c-ab33-3571-802b-9eeabd3be9d6", "product": {"name": "Apache Traffic Server", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "9.2.15"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "07596ae9-db7b-30ac-9fbd-23978170f3a3", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}], "isExploited": false}